WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.600
Ever since Dad died,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.130
the tanuki living in Kyoto have called 
us brothers from Tadasu no Mori

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.230
“idiots who failed to inherit 
their magnificent father's blood.”

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.220
And yeah, stuff those gossipy 
tanuki said behind our backs

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.280
might have hit the mark at times.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:24.540
But saying it as if our dad's blood went off 
somewhere and disappeared into thin air,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.540
that <i>really</i> pisses me off.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.550
In the first place, all tanuki 
are idiots to some extent.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.550
Going a step further, I'd 
say there's no better proof

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:39.290
that we inherited our dad's blood 
than the fact that we're idiots.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.850
After reaching the apex of tanuki society,

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.970
Dad's idiocy took a turn, 
and he ascended to a state of hot pot.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.030
<b>Episode 11: 
Back in the Game</b>

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.540
Can we get you to just give 
up and come with us, Yasaburo?

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.040
What are you doing, Ebisugawa?

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.660
Awful rain we're having.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.500
Benten, happy to find you in good humor.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.090
Pretty sure I'm telling 
you I'm <i>not</i> in good humor.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:25.250
I was waiting out the rain up 
there when I saw you, Yasaburo.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.010
Thought I'd have you transform 
into an umbrella for me.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:32.440
If it's for you, Benten, I'd transform into 
an umbrella or anything else for that matter.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.670
But...

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:38.590
What, Ebisugawa? You have 
a problem with that?

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.870
We were just about to head 
to a reconciliation banquet.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.710
If you were to take him away

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.720
I would find myself 
in quite a predicament.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.590
You say you'd find yourself in a predicament, 
but I wonder what that has to do with me?

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.470
You mean I should go home 
as I am and get sopping wet?

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.470
No, no, not at all.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.740
Then I'll just borrow him for a bit.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.270
Awful weather, huh.

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:29.240
You saved me. Thank you.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.020
Did I do something?

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.100
No thank-yous necessary.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.130
I went to Master's room the day 
before yesterday, on Christmas Eve.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.550
What for?

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.270
I got drunk for the first time in a while,

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.420
so I thought it wouldn't be 
so bad to check in on him.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.100
He was sleeping like a rock, 
though, so I went home right away.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:55.570
You gave him that cane, right?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.720
No present for me?

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.070
No.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.360
Why not?

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.060
There's nothing you want, is there?

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.130
You're powerful enough to 
get whatever you're after.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.420
That's a horrible thing to say.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.000
I haven't gotten a single thing I want.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.050
You're pretty quiet today, huh.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.980
I know you put Father in 
a cage for Ebisugawa...

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.900
Why didn't you ever say anything?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.210
Huh?

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.280
You never asked!

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.030
Dammit, you humans really are so nasty…

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.530
I'm a tengu!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.420
Nope, you're a human. No 
matter what you do, human.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.890
So you were mad about that and 
giving me the silent treatment?

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.310
It's not just that.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.790
It seems my brothers have 
been captured by Ebisugawa.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.660
You know how today is the 
Friday Fellows' year-end bash.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:04.260
My big brother might be 
boiled in their hot pot.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.140
Good heavens!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:10.360
So tonight I'll eat your big brother?

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.520
How terrible!

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.880
Would you be able to save him for me?

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:17.170
I dunno about that.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:21.350
Why? Because he's a tanuki, 
you won't save him?

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.610
Well, I <i>am</i> a human.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.480
Well then I'll do something 
about it on my own.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.710
Where are the Friday Fellows 
having their thing?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.090
Chitose-ya in Pontocho.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:39.980
But do me a favor and don't charge 
in there with your fists flying.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.380
You're so quick to resort to 
violence like that; I hate it.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:53.010
Prof. Yodogawa was saying he would 
go claim the tanuki this afternoon.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:58.760
He said he's in touch with someone who 
caught one and they made an agreement.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.820
Ahh right, Prof. Yodogawa…

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:09.590
Figure the rest out by yourself.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:14.800
I'm a human, so I just eat the 
tanuki that end up a hot pot.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.500
Couldn't care less.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.470
Prof. Yodogawa!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.440
Special delivery!

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.060
This is it! Divine grace!

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.570
<b>Chikurintei Soba</b>

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.090
Excuse me!

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:04.820
Excuse me!

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.270
I'll have an egg bowl.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.280
Let me outta here!

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.700
Dammit!

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.600
Yaichiro, is that you?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.500
Mother!

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.000
Mother!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.130
Yaichiro, you got caught, too?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.350
Mother, I'll save you!

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.570
Ugh, I can't get out!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.930
Once you're put in a cage, there's 
nothing you can do, Yaichiro.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.400
You tried to get to me because 
Raijin showed up, didn't you?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.100
It's my fault.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:07.570
This all happened because 
I'm so scared of thunder.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.230
None of that matters!

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:13.040
I wonder what happened 
to Yasaburo and Yashiro.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.910
As long as they're not having 
too rough of a time...

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.770
This is an Ebisugawa conspiracy!

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.110
He's a tanuki! How can he do this?!

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:23.900
Go to hell!

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.960
Are you okay, Mother?

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:29.420
I'm just a bit cold.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.010
That's strange.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.240
“Back in the game, you know my name.”

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.170
Yashiro?

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:11.920
We're back in the game!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.720
<b>Back in the game</b>

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.720
<b>Back in the game</b>

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.920
You poisoned the egg bowl?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.520
We tricked him good, huh, Big Brother!

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.970
Well done, Ginkaku.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.650
Go to h--

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.030
Gentlemen,

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:43.010
the day of vindication has arrived!

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.040
Yay!

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.040
<b>Chikurintei</b>

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.040
<b>Demachi 
shopping arcade</b>

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.040
<b>Masugata Co-op</b>

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.340
It's ready to go in here.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.490
How many do you need, Jurojin?

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.560
Benten will be there,

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:17.020
so we need to prepare enough for ten people.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.320
Oh my,

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.540
if it isn't the tanuki, here, of all places.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:28.230
Yes, I made an agreement to turn 
him over for tonight's banquet.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:32.920
Ah, so Hotei asked someone 
else to get one for him...

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.930
How pathetic.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.410
This weakness for tanuki

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.740
Hotei's had lately is really no good.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:45.110
That's where I come in.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:49.170
You do that kind of business 
as well, hmm, Ebisugawa?

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.860
What an utterly wicked fellow you are.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.690
Thanks.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.700
So there'll be two tanuki tonight?

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.860
Splendid!

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.460
Ahh, not this one, not this one.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.660
Oh, just one?

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.380
Even if you yourself ordered it, Jurojin,

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.500
I can't give up this tanuki.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:15.140
You mean you're fond of this one?

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.560
Yes, it's as you say.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.530
Well, that's fine.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.420
Take this to Chitose-ya.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.640
Understood.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.240
Crap!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.030
I'm not about to let them 
boil you in a hot pot!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:39.950
But there's nothing we can do at the moment.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:45.160
If there's anyone who can 
save us, it's Yasaburo,

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.560
but he's probably been captured as well.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:51.940
If he weren't, there's no way 
Soun could be that laid back.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.930
We can't give up!

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:57.720
Yasaburo is sharp and fearless,

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.940
so I'm sure we'll be okay.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.920
Hey, Kinkaku, let me outta here!

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:06.690
How about transforming 
if you're so good at it?

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:10.000
Oh, you can't if you're locked up like that?

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:15.050
That's right, Big Brother. To transform 
you gotta have "inner calm."

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:17.090
Right, right.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:20.600
At the moment he doesn't have 
a shred of inner calm, does he?

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:22.560
Too bad!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.630
You rotten jerks are a disgrace 
to all tanuki society!

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:31.070
Are you... Could it be you're an<i> idiot</i>?

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:33.540
He must be an idiot, Big Brother.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:38.790
Being an idiot, you probably don't even 
realize what's happened to you! So I'll tell you.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:44.730
I predicted you would follow Prof. 
Yodogawa to try to save Yaichiro.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.230
Predicted!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:50.720
Even so, no matter how 
brilliant my transformation,

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:54.720
you must be blind as a bat if you couldn't 
tell he was a fake Prof. Yodogawa.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:57.110
Aren't you friends with him?

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:01.820
Kinkaku, Ginkaku! When I get outta this cage 
I'm gonna bust your asses into eight cheeks!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.830
Sixteen between you!

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:06.060
Addition? Whatever.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:09.030
It might be multiplication, Big Brother.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:11.190
Hmm? Two times eight is sixt--

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:12.540
Well either way!

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.970
We're wearing iron underwear made reluctantly

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.850
by an artisan blacksmith in Nagahama, 
so we're cool as cucumbers!

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.450
Cool as cucumbers! Cool as cucumbers!

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:23.380
We even stuck hand warmers in 'em 
so our butts won't get cold.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.740
This foolproof plan... I must be a genius!

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.220
Heaven's vengeance is slow but sure!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.530
This was all Big Brother's original idea.

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:35.050
Meticulous planning! Meticulous planning!

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.300
Have you given up, Yasaburo?

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:41.150
What? No way, I'm not giving up yet.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:45.000
You stubborn jackass!

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.160
This is a plan I've been 
carefully putting together

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.780
using my <i>clear</i> head since<i> last year</i>!

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:55.680
Pitiful Yaichiro, our father is turning 
him over to Prof. Yodogawa, right?

00:12:55.950 --> 00:13:01.330
Your tail-popping little brother is in 
a warehouse at the Electric Brandy factory,

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:06.180
but we locked it up with a padlock as big as a kagami mochi, so no matter what, he can't escape.

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:09.270
We've also got your mother.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:14.140
And you're here, crammed in a 
cage inside Ginkaku's stomach.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.550
Still not giving up?

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:19.120
Who's gonna save you, and how?

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:21.350
Yajiro is still out there!

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.380
Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:28.010
You're so stupid! What are you 
saying that frog-in-a-well can do?

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:30.370
The Shimogama family is broken.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.890
All we have to do now is 
wait for the sun to go down.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:38.970
Rest in peace. Soon-to-be-hot-pot 
Yaichiro, may you attain nirvana.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.670
Rest in peace, rest in peace.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:46.420
Argh! No matter how much of an idiot you 
are, there's still such a thing as good and bad!

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:50.130
I don't want to get lectured 
by a dope like you.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:54.040
Yaichiro ascends to hot pot and 
our father ascends to Nise-emon.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:57.670
And then down the line I'll 
inherit the title of Nise-emon.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:03.330
The clever, strong, young hope who will 
shoulder the future of tanuki society is me!

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:04.430
Quite right!

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:05.690
Quite right!

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.120
Let's talk 'til the battery runs out…

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:20.670
Oh, Kaisei? It's your big bro.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:25.050
Hold tight 'til tonight, would ya?

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:30.800
No, you can't now. We're at Chikurintei 
teaching Yasaburo a less--

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:34.860
I'm beggin' ya, don't talk like that.

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:37.180
Your big bro's feelings'll get all hurt.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.420
I hope they do and that it kills you!

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:45.370
C'mon, don't say that. 
You're an unmarried girl.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:49.480
Right? So take better care of yourself.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.620
Then quit screwin' aro--

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:56.590
I'm just lookin' out for her…

00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:00.830
Your little sister doesn't have 
any respect for you at all!

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.660
Right, thanks!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:03.960
Thanks!

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:08.520
Mother!

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:13.030
Mother, are you all right?

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.980
You're not cold, are you?

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.200
Mother!

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:24.930
I'm all right. I'm not cold.

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:29.630
You weren't moving a muscle so I got worried.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:32.840
I'm conserving energy.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.770
Struggling'll only end in a sore bottom.

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.490
The professor has arrived.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.960
Once I turn you over, I'm going to Sensuiro.

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:56.140
You can just leave the future 
of tanuki society to me.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.780
Farewell, Yaichiro. Quietly 
accept the hot pot.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:02.230
Go to hell!

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.230
You think I'm gonna let you have your way?

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.040
I'm not gonna be boiled 
in a hot pot so easily!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:12.190
I've got your mother in the palm of my hand.

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:15.120
If you were to run, what would happen to her?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.150
How dirty do you have to 
play before you're happy?!

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:21.370
Say what you want-- I don't give a damn.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.640
Mr. Ebisugawa.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.080
You've changed this much, huh?

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.780
I think it's an awful shame.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.630
I'm sure So would think so, too.

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:38.720
If So knew his little brother had become such 
a horrible tanuki, he would be crushed.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:43.890
So? He already knew.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.710
Tanuki don't do horrible things like this.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:51.760
It's like something a tengu or 
a human would do, Mr. Ebisugawa!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.150
Mr. Ebisugawa,

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:58.730
I'm begging you, please 
stop bullying my children.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.840
You call me “Ebisugawa."

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.630
But you're Ebisugawa.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:12.300
Then what do the children of you 
and my brother have to do with me?

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.220
If you have a chance to run, 
do it and don't worry about me!

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.840
Mother!

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:32.420
Hello there.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.340
So this is the one.

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.490
Yes, here he is, as we agreed.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.490
What a magnificent lil' guy.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:46.240
But you know, tonight we're gonna eat you up.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:18:59.850
That's...

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:34.380
Yashiro!

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:36.620
Yashiro!

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:41.540
Kaisei, get me outta here!

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:43.840
I can't, it's locked.

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:47.260
But I gotta hurry!

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:49.270
I know, calm down.

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:52.980
There's a hidden door in the corner 
of the warehouse; look for it.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:55.750
If you undo the latch from 
the inside, you can get out.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:04.870
Thanks!

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.010
Where are my brothers?

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:09.480
Yaichiro was captured by the Friday Fellows.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:14.160
Kinkaku said on the phone earlier that he 
and Ginkaku are teaching Yasaburo a lesson…

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.150
And Mother? Is Mother here, too?

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:21.270
She was captured, too, but 
she's not at the factory.

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:24.630
My dad must have her 
locked up somewhere else.

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:27.250
Maybe at the Electric Brandy shop.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.290
These guys are so cruel!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.080
If we can save Yasaburo, 
it'll all work out somehow.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.290
This won't do, Young Mistress.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.880
Now please return to your room.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.000
We'll be scolded by Master Soun!

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:40.400
Run.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:42.720
Young Mistress!

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:56.440
Go to Chikurintei!

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:00.670
If I go by myself Kinkaku and 
Ginkaku will beat me to a pulp.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:05.070
Come with and tell 'em off for me!

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:08.330
If I go with you, all of 
these guys will be after us.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.830
You're going alone!

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:18.520
Put your tail away and run for it!

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.010
Achieving sublimity in idiocy--

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:26.540
we take pride in it.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:32.440
As the manifestion of the idiot blood 
flowing through the veins of our dad,

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:36.560
and his dad, and generations 
of the Shimogamo family,

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:40.630
sometimes we trick humans, 
sometimes we harass tengu,

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:44.210
sometimes we fall into a boiling iron pot.

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:49.840
These aren't things to be ashamed of, 
but things of which we should be proud.

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:55.440
We brothers must know that 
there is honor in having pride,

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:58.550
even and especially if our 
eyes are full of tears.

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:34.600
Being in a tiny cage makes you feel helpless,

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:37.230
but if anyone can get 
through this, it's my kids!

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:39.300
Right? I just know it.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>The False Eizan 
Electric Railway</b>
